+//! `UploadPart`'s **commit half** (#927, the second of #657's two slices; the first is
+//! [`super::stage`]): turn a staged attempt into a committed part, or into a compensated loss,
+//! and compose the whole verb, reserve → stage → commit ([`upload_part`]). Proposal 0016's *Part
+//! commit* and *Live-session compensation* rows (`0016:660`, `:673`) and decision 5's commit
+//! classification and quiesce rule (`0016:1584-1653`, `:1720-1733`).
+//!
+//! | Batch | Preconditions | Mutations |
+//! |---|---|---|
+//! | part commit | `require(mpu:<id> == Open@E)`, `require_absent(part:<id>:<n>)` or `require(part:<id>:<n> == prior)`, `require(slot:<id>:<k> == the bytes this attempt last wrote)`, and for a re-upload over a non-empty prior `require_absent(retire:bytes:s:<id>:<E>:<n>:<attempt>)` | put `part:`, put its `psum:` summary, delete the slot, delete every owned `sidx:` entry, and for that re-upload put the `{chunks}` obligation naming the **prior** part's chunks |
+//! | compensation | `require(mpu:<id> == Open@E)` (the epoch it compensates under, possibly a newer one than the commit's), `require(slot:<id>:<k> == the bytes this attempt last wrote)`, and for a non-empty part `require_absent` of its obligation key | delete the slot, delete every owned `sidx:` entry, and for a non-empty part put the `{chunks}` obligation naming **this attempt's own** chunks |
+//!
+//! An obligation names at least one chunk (`RetireObligation` refuses an empty list), so an
+//! empty part, or a re-upload over an empty prior, installs none, and its slot release and
+//! owned-entry deletes ride in the same batch all the same.
+//!
+//! # Quiesce, then commit
+//!
+//! The attempt's last renewal ([`StagedAttempt::renew`]) runs first, with a lease covering
+//! [`COMMIT_COVER_MILLIS`], the commit's transaction deadline; no renewal is sent after it, so the
+//! only writer of the slot until the commit lands is the commit itself (`0016:1720-1733`). Its
+//! typed coverage error ends the call before any commit is sent. Then two reads: the bounded
+//! `psum:<id>:` range, for the cumulative ceiling, and the part key. Then one batch.
+//!
+//! # A commit that did not say `Committed`
+//!
+//! Never read as `Conflict`, never compensated blind. After every commit that did not land, four
+//! reads, in this order: the part key, the session, the attempt's own slot, the session again.
+//! Each answers one question, and the order is what makes the answers hold:
+//!
+//! * **Own commit** — the slot gone (absent, or holding another attempt's id, `SlotRecord`'s
+//!   `attempt_id`) and the session read *after* it still the `Open@E` bytes the commit required,
+//!   while a commit of this attempt is in doubt: only this attempt's own commit can have done
+//!   that. While a session is `Open@E`, the writers of slot index `k` are this attempt and, once
+//!   it released the index, whichever later attempt reserves it; no reaper touches an `Open`
+//!   session (`0016:1625-1628`). That proof is checked **first**, whatever the part key holds:
+//!   `PartRecord` names no attempt, and an empty part names no chunk either, so the part's bytes
+//!   never prove whose commit they are.
+//! * **Settled, not landed** — the slot still at the bytes this attempt last wrote, and every
+//!   commit of it in doubt unable to land from then on: out of flight
+//!   (`may_still_commit: false`), or held while a read *before* the slot read found a
+//!   precondition of it that can never hold again (the session no longer `Open@E`, since an
+//!   epoch only rises; or the part key no longer what the commit requires, when that value
+//!   cannot come back: the key was required absent and is now present, or a non-empty prior is
+//!   gone, whose chunk ids no later write carries). An empty prior's bytes can come back (an
+//!   empty rival in the same millisecond writes them again), so a rival's empty record settles
+//!   nothing.
+//! * Until a held commit is settled, the attempt re-reads and retries **the same batch**, which
+//!   requires the same slot bytes, so at most one of them lands. It never compensates
+//!   (`0016:1649-1651`). When its rounds run out it returns [`CommitError::InDoubt`] with
+//!   `may_still_commit`, as `abort::abort_session` does.
+//!
+//! Once settled, the classification of a lost commit (`0016:1597-1647`):
+//!
+//! | The session (last read) | The part key | Answer |
+//! |---|---|---|
+//! | still `Open@E` | what the commit requires | a conflict no read explains (on TiKV, a lock another writer held): retry |
+//! | still `Open@E` | moved: a same-number rival won | compensate under `Open@E`; [`Refusal::OperationAborted`] |
+//! | back at a newer `Open@E'` (a Complete fenced and rolled back) | any | compensate under `Open@E'`; [`Refusal::OperationAborted`] |
+//! | not `Open`, or gone | any | [`Refusal::NoSuchUpload`]; the slot and the owned entries are the reaper's, whose walk covers every non-`Open` state |
+//!
+//! A slot found gone while the session has moved proves nothing about whose batch removed it (a
+//! teardown can), so with a commit in doubt that is [`CommitError::InDoubt`], never `Committed`
+//! and never a compensation.
+//!
+//! # Compensation
+//!
+//! Sent only once the commit is settled as not landed and unable to land later, so the slot
+//! compare-and-set it carries can only ever be decided against this attempt's compensations.
+//! An unknown outcome is settled by re-reading, in order, its obligation (when it has one), its
+//! own slot, then the session: the obligation holding the bytes it put, or the slot gone while
+//! the session is still the bytes a doubtful compensation required, means it landed. A
+//! compensation that lost to the session moving to a newer `Open` epoch is sent again under that
+//! epoch (the epoch chase, `0016:1607-1620`); one that finds the session no longer `Open` stops
+//! there, the residue the reaper's. With `may_still_commit: true` the doubt is kept as for the
+//! commit.
+//!
+//! # Every batch requires the slot bytes this attempt last wrote
+//!
+//! Both builders take the slot bytes from the attempt's own state ([`StagedAttempt::slot_bytes`],
+//! which its last renewal updated), never from a read of the key. So a slot index another attempt
+//! has since reserved is never required, rewritten or deleted by this one.
+//!
+//! # Bounds
+//!
+//! | Loop | At most |
+//! |---|---|
+//! | the quiesce renewal | `stage::RENEWAL_ROUNDS` commits |
+//! | part commit, retries of a held or unexplained one included | [`COMMIT_ROUNDS`] commits |
+//! | compensation, the epoch chase included | [`COMPENSATION_ROUNDS`] commits |
+//!
+//! Each round is followed by at most four reads (compensation: one per obligation it sent, then
+//! two). Each store call is bounded by the store's own contract.
+//!
+//! # The cumulative ceiling is a read, not a fence
+//!
+//! The `psum:` read is unfenced on purpose: concurrent commits of different part numbers may both
+//! read the same headroom and both commit, and the overshoot that leaves is bounded by the
+//! in-flight cap, `MAX_INFLIGHT_PARTS × MAX_PART_CHUNKS`, and charged in `U_REF`
+//! (`0016:1441-1451`). No counter or session-wide precondition joins the batch (`0016:1686-1742`).
+//!
+//! # One clock (ADR-0009)
+//!
+//! The quiesce renewal and the part's `committed_at_millis` stamp read the caller's
+//! [`StageClock`], the clock that owns the attempt's lease lifecycle and that staging ran on
+//! ([`super::stage`]'s "One clock"). Nothing else here reads a clock.
+//!
+//! No production path calls this module yet: the S3 `UploadPart` verb is #669, and the part
+//! records it writes are consumed by Complete (#658). The tests drive every branch over a real
+//! store with each interleaving forced by a scripted wrapper
+//! (`crates/core/tests/multipart_upload_part_commit.rs`); seeded DST coverage of the races is
+//! #660.
+
+// deferred: #660 — seeded Tier-0 DST coverage of the commit and compensation races (a commit
+// against a rival, an Abort, a Complete's rollback, the reaper), as for staging (`stage.rs`).
+
+use std::fmt;
+
+use bytes::Bytes;
+use futures_util::Stream;
+use wyrd_traits::{
+    BoxError, CommitOutcome, CommitUnknownResult, MetadataStore, PlacementChunkStore, WriteBatch,
+};
+
+use super::stage::{
+    stage_part, RenewOutcome, StageClock, StageError, StageOutcome, StageRequest, StageRuntime,
+    StagedAttempt,
+};
+use super::{
+    decode_part_record, decode_part_summary, decode_session_record, decode_slot_record, mpu_key,
+    parse_psum_key, part_key, psum_key, psum_range, upload_part_answer, PartRecord, RecordError,
+    Refusal, RetireObligation, UploadId, UploadPartAnswer, UploadPartOutcome, E_TX_MILLIS,
+    MAX_COMPLETE_ATTEMPTS,
+};
+use crate::metadata;
+
+/// The cover the commit asks of its quiesce renewal: the commit's transaction deadline, `E_tx`'s
+/// five seconds (`0016:1726-1728`), so no lease of the attempt can lapse under the commit. A
+/// request staged with a lease TTL not above it cannot be committed: the renewal refuses a cover
+/// it could not give.
+pub const COMMIT_COVER_MILLIS: u64 = E_TX_MILLIS;
+
+/// The most part-commit batches one [`commit_part`] sends: its first, and three more for a
+/// conflict no read explains (on TiKV, a lock another writer held), or for retrying a commit whose
+/// outcome the store could not report and no read has yet settled. A commit shares no writable
+/// key with an unrelated part (`0016:1597-1610`), so nothing else can make it lose and no round
+/// is spent on one.
+pub const COMMIT_ROUNDS: u32 = 4;
+
+/// The most compensation batches one [`commit_part`] sends: [`MAX_COMPLETE_ATTEMPTS`] `+ 1`, the
+/// budget `abort::ABORT_ROUNDS` takes and for the same reason. A session goes back to a newer
+/// `Open` epoch only when a Complete fence is released, at most [`MAX_COMPLETE_ATTEMPTS`] times,
+/// so the epoch chase costs at most that many rounds; the one more is the round that lands. A
+/// conflict no read explains and an unknown outcome share the budget.
+pub const COMPENSATION_ROUNDS: u32 = MAX_COMPLETE_ATTEMPTS + 1;
+
+/// Which of the attempt's batches a [`CommitError::InDoubt`] is about.
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub enum DoubtfulBatch {
+    /// The part commit: the part may be committed, or may still be.
+    Commit,
+    /// The live-session compensation: the obligation may be installed and the slot released, or
+    /// may still be.
+    Compensation,
+}
+
+/// A part commit that ended with neither an outcome nor a refusal.
+///
+/// # Error class
+///
+/// [`wyrd_traits::classify`] reads [`Self::InDoubt`] as
+/// [`ErrorClass::Indeterminate`](wyrd_traits::ErrorClass::Indeterminate): its
+/// [`source`](std::error::Error::source) is the store's own [`CommitUnknownResult`].
+/// [`Self::Stopped`] keeps its cause's class, and [`Self::Renewal`] its renewal error's.
+#[derive(Debug)]
+pub enum CommitError {
+    /// The quiesce renewal ([`StagedAttempt::renew`]) did not cover the commit, so no commit was
+    /// sent: its error, its doubt about its own rounds kept. What the attempt staged stays for the
+    /// reaper, as after any staging stop.
+    Renewal(StageError),
+    /// A batch of this attempt may have landed, or may still land, and the commit stopped before a
+    /// read could say which. Never "nothing was written".
+    InDoubt(Box<InDoubt>),
+    /// The commit stopped, and no batch of it is in doubt.
+    Stopped {
+        /// The session.
+        upload_id: UploadId,
+        /// What stopped it.
+        cause: Stop,
+    },
+}
+
+/// What a [`CommitError::InDoubt`] reports.
+#[derive(Debug)]
+pub struct InDoubt {
+    /// The session.
+    pub upload_id: UploadId,
+    /// Which batch is in doubt.
+    pub batch: DoubtfulBatch,
+    /// Whether that batch may still be applied **after** the call returned: one whose store report
+    /// said `may_still_commit` and whose required session bytes were still in place at the last
+    /// read. `false` for a batch that may have landed but no longer can (out of flight, or the
+    /// session it required has moved on, which an epoch never undoes).
+    pub may_still_commit: bool,
+    /// The store's report that keeps the doubt: the first that said `may_still_commit` of a batch
+    /// that may still land, or else the latest no read has settled. It is the error's
+    /// [`source`](std::error::Error::source).
+    pub outcome: CommitUnknownResult,
+    /// What stopped the commit before it could settle the doubt.
+    pub cause: Stop,
+}
+
+/// What stopped a part commit ([`CommitError::Stopped`], [`InDoubt::cause`]).
+#[derive(Debug)]
+pub enum Stop {
+    /// All [`COMMIT_ROUNDS`] commits were sent without one landing or being settled as lost.
+    CommitRoundsSpent {
+        /// Commits sent.
+        rounds: u32,
+    },
+    /// All [`COMPENSATION_ROUNDS`] compensations were sent without one landing.
+    CompensationRoundsSpent {
+        /// Compensations sent.
+        rounds: u32,
+    },
+    /// The session moved off the bytes the doubtful batch required while the attempt's slot was
+    /// gone: the batch may have landed before it moved, and a teardown can remove a slot too, so
+    /// no read can say which.
+    SessionMoved,
+    /// The attempt's slot is gone, or rewritten under this attempt's id, and no batch of this
+    /// attempt explains it: something other than this attempt removed or rewrote it while the
+    /// session was live.
+    SlotLost {
+        /// The slot key, as UTF-8 (lossy).
+        key: String,
+    },
+    /// The compensation's obligation key holds bytes this attempt did not put. A token is minted
+    /// once (`0016:358-373`), so this is damage a retry cannot settle.
+    ObligationKeyTaken {
+        /// The `retire:` key, as UTF-8 (lossy).
+        key: String,
+    },
+    /// A stored record is not valid (ADR-0045), or a value this attempt would write is not one its
+    /// decoder accepts.
+    Record(RecordError),
+    /// A metadata store operation failed.
+    Store(BoxError),
+}
+
+impl fmt::Display for CommitError {
+    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
+        match self {
+            Self::Renewal(err) => write!(
+                f,
+                "multipart part commit: the quiesce renewal did not cover the commit, so none was \
+                 sent: {err}"
+            ),
+            Self::InDoubt(doubt) => write!(
+                f,
+                "multipart part commit: upload {} is in doubt: this attempt's {} {} ({})",
+                doubt.upload_id,
+                match doubt.batch {
+                    DoubtfulBatch::Commit => "part commit",
+                    DoubtfulBatch::Compensation => "compensation",
+                },
+                if doubt.may_still_commit {
+                    "may still be applied"
+                } else {
+                    "may have been applied"
+                },
+                doubt.cause,
+            ),
+            Self::Stopped { upload_id, cause } => write!(
+                f,
+                "multipart part commit: upload {upload_id}: {cause}; no batch of this part attempt \
+                 is in doubt"
+            ),
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+impl fmt::Display for Stop {
+    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
+        match self {
+            Self::CommitRoundsSpent { rounds } => {
+                write!(
+                    f,
+                    "all {rounds} part commits were spent without one landing"
+                )
+            }
+            Self::CompensationRoundsSpent { rounds } => {
+                write!(
+                    f,
+                    "all {rounds} compensations were spent without one landing"
+                )
+            }
+            Self::SessionMoved => f.write_str(
+                "the session moved off the bytes the batch required while the attempt's slot was \
+                 gone, so no read can say whether the batch landed first",
+            ),
+            Self::SlotLost { key } => write!(
+                f,
+                "the slot {key} was removed or rewritten by something other than this attempt"
+            ),
+            Self::ObligationKeyTaken { key } => write!(
+                f,
+                "the obligation key {key} holds bytes this attempt did not put; this is damage a \
+                 retry cannot settle"
+            ),
+            Self::Record(err) => write!(f, "invalid record: {err}"),
+            Self::Store(err) => write!(f, "store fault: {err}"),
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+impl std::error::Error for CommitError {
+    fn source(&self) -> Option<&(dyn std::error::Error + 'static)> {
+        match self {
+            Self::Renewal(err) => Some(err),
+            // The unknown outcome, never the stop cause: `classify` stops at the first seam type
+            // on the chain, and a doubtful commit must read `Indeterminate`.
+            Self::InDoubt(doubt) => Some(&doubt.outcome),
+            Self::Stopped { cause, .. } => match cause {
+                Stop::Record(err) => Some(err),
+                Stop::Store(err) => Some(err.as_ref()),
+                Stop::CommitRoundsSpent { .. }
+                | Stop::CompensationRoundsSpent { .. }
+                | Stop::SessionMoved
+                | Stop::SlotLost { .. }
+                | Stop::ObligationKeyTaken { .. } => None,
+            },
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/// What the composed [`upload_part`] ended with, when it ended with neither an outcome nor a
+/// refusal: staging's error, or the commit's. Each keeps its own class ([`StageError`],
+/// [`CommitError`]).
+#[derive(Debug)]
+pub enum UploadPartError {
+    /// Staging stopped ([`stage_part`]); no commit was attempted.
+    Stage(StageError),
+    /// The commit stopped ([`commit_part`]).
+    Commit(CommitError),
+}
+
+impl fmt::Display for UploadPartError {
+    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
+        match self {
+            Self::Stage(err) => write!(f, "{err}"),
+            Self::Commit(err) => write!(f, "{err}"),
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+impl std::error::Error for UploadPartError {
+    fn source(&self) -> Option<&(dyn std::error::Error + 'static)> {
+        match self {
+            Self::Stage(err) => Some(err),
+            Self::Commit(err) => Some(err),
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/// One batch of this attempt whose outcome the store could not report.
+#[derive(Debug)]
+struct Unsure {
+    outcome: CommitUnknownResult,
+    /// The `mpu:` bytes the batch required.
+    session: Bytes,
+    /// Whether it may still land: the store said `may_still_commit`, and no read since has found
+    /// one of its preconditions gone for good.
+    may_land: bool,
+}
+
+/// What one phase knows about its own batches whose outcome the store could not report. Every
+/// such batch deletes the attempt's slot at the bytes it last wrote, so a read finding the slot
+/// still there settles every one that can no longer land.
+#[derive(Debug, Default)]
+struct Doubt(Vec<Unsure>);
+
+impl Doubt {
+    fn observe(&mut self, outcome: &CommitUnknownResult, session: &Bytes) {
+        self.0.push(Unsure {
+            outcome: outcome.clone(),
+            session: session.clone(),
+            may_land: outcome.may_still_commit,
+        });
+    }
+
+    /// A read found the session at `found`: a batch that required other bytes can never land
+    /// from now on (an epoch only rises), though it may have landed before.
+    fn session_seen(&mut self, found: Option<&Bytes>) {
+        for unsure in &mut self.0 {
+            if found != Some(&unsure.session) {
+                unsure.may_land = false;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// A read found a precondition every batch in doubt carries gone for good.
+    fn cannot_land(&mut self) {
+        for unsure in &mut self.0 {
+            unsure.may_land = false;
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// A read found the slot still at the bytes every batch in doubt deletes: none of them has
+    /// landed, and one that can no longer land never will.
+    fn slot_held(&mut self) {
+        self.0.retain(|unsure| unsure.may_land);
+    }
+
+    fn any(&self) -> bool {
+        !self.0.is_empty()
+    }
+
+    /// Whether a batch in doubt required exactly the session bytes `found`.
+    fn required(&self, found: Option<&Bytes>) -> bool {
+        self.0.iter().any(|unsure| found == Some(&unsure.session))
+    }
+
+    fn end(self, upload_id: &UploadId, batch: DoubtfulBatch, cause: Stop) -> CommitError {
+        let keep = self
+            .0
+            .iter()
+            .find(|unsure| unsure.may_land)
+            .or_else(|| self.0.last());
+        match keep {
+            Some(unsure) => CommitError::InDoubt(Box::new(InDoubt {
+                upload_id: upload_id.clone(),
+                batch,
+                may_still_commit: unsure.may_land,
+                outcome: unsure.outcome.clone(),
+                cause,
+            })),
+            None => stopped(upload_id, cause),
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+fn stopped(upload_id: &UploadId, cause: Stop) -> CommitError {
+    CommitError::Stopped {
+        upload_id: upload_id.clone(),
+        cause,
+    }
+}
+
+fn lossy(key: &[u8]) -> String {
+    String::from_utf8_lossy(key).into_owned()
+}
+
+/// What a read of the attempt's own slot found.
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
+enum SlotSeen {
+    /// The bytes this attempt last wrote.
+    Held,
+    /// Absent, or another attempt's slot: this attempt's slot is gone.
+    Gone,
+    /// This attempt's id, under bytes it did not last write.
+    Rewritten,
+}
+
+/// Judge a read of the slot. A stored slot that does not decode is an error (ADR-0045), never
+/// "another attempt's".
+fn judge_slot(found: Option<&Bytes>, attempt: &StagedAttempt) -> Result<SlotSeen, RecordError> {
+    let Some(bytes) = found else {
+        return Ok(SlotSeen::Gone);
+    };
+    if bytes == attempt.slot_bytes() {
+        return Ok(SlotSeen::Held);
+    }
+    let record = decode_slot_record(bytes)?;
+    Ok(if record.attempt_id() == attempt.attempt_id() {
+        SlotSeen::Rewritten
+    } else {
+        SlotSeen::Gone
+    })
+}
+
+/// What a read of the session found, against the bytes a batch required.
+enum SessionSeen {
+    /// Those bytes.
+    Same,
+    /// Another `Open` session record: a newer epoch.
+    Open(Bytes),
+    /// Not `Open`, or no record: the answer its state gives.
+    Left(Refusal),
+}
+
+fn judge_session(found: Option<&Bytes>, required: &Bytes) -> Result<SessionSeen, RecordError> {
+    let Some(bytes) = found else {
+        return Ok(SessionSeen::Left(Refusal::NoSuchUpload));
+    };
+    if bytes == required {
+        return Ok(SessionSeen::Same);
+    }
+    let record = decode_session_record(bytes)?;
+    Ok(match upload_part_answer(Some(record.state())) {
+        UploadPartAnswer::Accepted => SessionSeen::Open(bytes.clone()),
+        UploadPartAnswer::Refused(refusal) => SessionSeen::Left(refusal),
+    })
+}
+
+/// The chunks the session's committed parts hold, its own part number's prior excluded (a
+/// re-upload replaces it): the sum over the bounded `psum:<id>:` range of summaries, never the
+/// chunk lists (`0016:352`).
+async fn staged_elsewhere(
+    store: &impl MetadataStore,
+    attempt: &StagedAttempt,
+) -> Result<u64, Stop> {
+    let mut total = 0u64;
+    for (key, value) in store
+        .scan(&psum_range(attempt.upload_id()))
+        .await
+        .map_err(Stop::Store)?
+    {
+        let (_, part_number) = parse_psum_key(&key).map_err(Stop::Record)?;
+        if part_number == attempt.part_number() {
+            continue;
+        }
+        let summary = decode_part_summary(&value).map_err(Stop::Record)?;
+        total = total.saturating_add(u64::from(summary.chunks));
+    }
+    Ok(total)
+}
+
+/// The part commit's batch (`0016:660`).
+fn commit_batch(
+    attempt: &StagedAttempt,
+    session: &Bytes,
+    required: Option<&Bytes>,
+    record: &PartRecord,
+    retire: Option<&RetireObligation>,
+) -> WriteBatch {
+    let upload_id = attempt.upload_id();
+    let part = part_key(upload_id, attempt.part_number());
+    let mut batch = WriteBatch::new().require(mpu_key(upload_id), session.clone());
+    batch = match required {
+        Some(prior) => batch.require(part.clone(), prior.clone()),
+        None => batch.require_absent(part.clone()),
+    };
+    // The bytes this attempt last wrote, from its own state: never re-read from the key.
+    batch = batch.require(attempt.slot_key().to_vec(), attempt.slot_bytes().clone());
+    if let Some(obligation) = retire {
+        batch = batch.require_absent(obligation.key());
+    }
+    batch = batch
+        .put(part, metadata::encode(record))
+        .put(
+            psum_key(upload_id, attempt.part_number()),
+            metadata::encode(&record.summary()),
+        )
+        .delete(attempt.slot_key().to_vec());
+    for owned in attempt.owned() {
+        batch = batch.delete(owned.key().to_vec());
+    }
+    if let Some(obligation) = retire {
+        batch = batch.put(obligation.key(), metadata::encode(obligation.payload()));
+    }
+    batch
+}
+
+/// The live-session compensation's batch (`0016:673`), under `session`.
+fn compensation_batch(
+    attempt: &StagedAttempt,
+    session: &Bytes,
+    obligation: Option<&RetireObligation>,
+) -> WriteBatch {
+    let mut batch = WriteBatch::new()
+        .require(mpu_key(attempt.upload_id()), session.clone())
+        // The bytes this attempt last wrote, from its own state: never re-read from the key.
+        .require(attempt.slot_key().to_vec(), attempt.slot_bytes().clone());
+    if let Some(obligation) = obligation {
+        batch = batch.require_absent(obligation.key());
+    }
+    batch = batch.delete(attempt.slot_key().to_vec());
+    for owned in attempt.owned() {
+        batch = batch.delete(owned.key().to_vec());
+    }
+    if let Some(obligation) = obligation {
+        batch = batch.put(obligation.key(), metadata::encode(obligation.payload()));
+    }
+    batch
+}
+
+/// **Commit a staged part** (`0016:660`, `:1584-1653`, `:1720-1733`), answering in the landed
+/// vocabulary ([`UploadPartOutcome`], [`Refusal`]). The module doc states the batches, the order of
+/// the reads, the classification and the bounds.
+///
+/// * A part whose staging stopped at the per-part chunk bound
+///   ([`StagedAttempt::chunk_bound_exceeded`]) is refused [`Refusal::EntityTooLarge`], its
+///   `chunks` one past the bound (the body was longer; staging did not read the rest) and its
+///   `limit` the bound, and what it staged is compensated.
+/// * Otherwise the quiesce renewal runs ([`COMMIT_COVER_MILLIS`]); a session it finds no longer
+///   `Open` is [`Refusal::NoSuchUpload`], with nothing more written.
+/// * A part that would take the session's committed chunks past `max_staged_chunks`
+///   ([`super::MAX_STAGED_CHUNKS`] at the shipped profile), counted over the `psum:` summaries of
+///   every other part number, is refused [`Refusal::EntityTooLarge`] (`chunks` the total it would
+///   reach, `limit` the ceiling) and compensated.
+/// * Otherwise one commit batch: [`UploadPartOutcome::Committed`] when it lands, or when a re-read
+///   proves this attempt's own commit landed; a lost commit compensates and answers
+///   [`Refusal::OperationAborted`] while the session is `Open`, and [`Refusal::NoSuchUpload`] once
+///   it is not.
+///
+/// `clock` must be the clock the attempt was staged on.
+///
+/// **Not cancel-safe once a commit is sent**: dropping the future can leave a batch that lands
+/// with no answer naming it. The slot and every owned entry it could leave are still in reach of
+/// the reaper's per-session ranges.
+pub async fn commit_part(
+    store: &impl MetadataStore,
+    clock: &impl StageClock,
+    mut attempt: StagedAttempt,
+    max_staged_chunks: u32,
+) -> Result<UploadPartOutcome, CommitError> {
+    let upload_id = attempt.upload_id().clone();
+    let stop = |cause| stopped(&upload_id, cause);
+    if attempt.chunk_bound_exceeded() {
+        let limit = attempt.chunks().len() as u64;
+        let refusal = Refusal::EntityTooLarge {
+            chunks: limit.saturating_add(1),
+            limit,
+        };
+        let session = attempt.session_bytes().clone();
+        return compensate(store, &attempt, session, refusal).await;
+    }
+    match attempt.renew(store, clock, COMMIT_COVER_MILLIS).await {
+        Ok(RenewOutcome::Covered { .. }) => {}
+        Ok(RenewOutcome::Refused(refusal)) => return Ok(UploadPartOutcome::Refused(refusal)),
+        Err(err) => return Err(CommitError::Renewal(err)),
+    }
+    // The commit's reads, after the last renewal: no renewal is sent from here on.
+    let total = staged_elsewhere(store, &attempt)
+        .await
+        .map_err(stop)?
+        .saturating_add(attempt.chunks().len() as u64);
+    if total > u64::from(max_staged_chunks) {
+        let refusal = Refusal::EntityTooLarge {
+            chunks: total,
+            limit: u64::from(max_staged_chunks),
+        };
+        let session = attempt.session_bytes().clone();
+        return compensate(store, &attempt, session, refusal).await;
+    }
+    let part = part_key(&upload_id, attempt.part_number());
+    let required = store
+        .get(&part)
+        .await
+        .map_err(|fault| stop(Stop::Store(fault)))?;
+    let prior = required
+        .as_deref()
+        .map(decode_part_record)
+        .transpose()
+        .map_err(|err| stop(Stop::Record(err)))?;
+    let session = attempt.session_bytes().clone();
+    let epoch = decode_session_record(&session)
+        .map_err(|err| stop(Stop::Record(err)))?
+        .epoch();
+    // `committed_at_millis` is stamped once, by the clock that owns the attempt's leases, so every
+    // retry of the commit puts the same bytes.
+    let record = PartRecord::commit(
+        attempt.chunks().to_vec(),
+        *attempt.digest(),
+        clock.now_millis(),
+        epoch,
+    )
+    .map_err(|err| stop(Stop::Record(err)))?;
+    let retire = match &prior {
+        Some(prior) => RetireObligation::part_chunks(
+            &upload_id,
+            epoch,
+            attempt.part_number(),
+            attempt.attempt_id(),
+            prior.chunks(),
+        )
+        .map_err(|err| stop(Stop::Record(err)))?,
+        None => None,
+    };
+    // A required value that can come back once moved: only an empty prior's, whose bytes an empty
+    // rival in the same millisecond and epoch writes again.
+    let can_recur = prior.as_ref().is_some_and(PartRecord::is_empty);
+    let batch = commit_batch(
+        &attempt,
+        &session,
+        required.as_ref(),
+        &record,
+        retire.as_ref(),
+    );
+    let committed = UploadPartOutcome::Committed {
+        part_number: attempt.part_number(),
+        digest: *attempt.digest(),
+    };
+    let session_key = mpu_key(&upload_id);
+    let read = |key: &[u8]| {
+        let key = key.to_vec();
+        async move { store.get(&key).await }
+    };
+    let mut doubt = Doubt::default();
+    let mut rounds = 0u32;
+    loop {
+        if rounds == COMMIT_ROUNDS {
+            return Err(doubt.end(
+                &upload_id,
+                DoubtfulBatch::Commit,
+                Stop::CommitRoundsSpent { rounds },
+            ));
+        }
+        rounds += 1;
+        match store.commit(batch.clone()).await {
+            Ok(CommitOutcome::Committed) => return Ok(committed),
+            Ok(CommitOutcome::Conflict) => {}
+            Err(fault) => match fault.downcast_ref::<CommitUnknownResult>() {
+                Some(unknown) => doubt.observe(unknown, &session),
+                // A definite failure of this batch; an earlier batch's doubt still stands.
+                None => {
+                    return Err(doubt.end(&upload_id, DoubtfulBatch::Commit, Stop::Store(fault)))
+                }
+            },
+        }
+        // Each read is its own transaction, so each is judged at the instant it was taken. Every
+        // read below is processed in order, and the order is the module doc's.
+        let fault =
+            |doubt: Doubt, fault| doubt.end(&upload_id, DoubtfulBatch::Commit, Stop::Store(fault));
+        let torn =
+            |doubt: Doubt, err| doubt.end(&upload_id, DoubtfulBatch::Commit, Stop::Record(err));
+        let part_now = match read(&part).await {
+            Ok(found) => found,
+            Err(err) => return Err(fault(doubt, err)),
+        };
+        if part_now != required && !can_recur {
+            // The part key no longer holds what every commit requires, and that value never comes
+            // back: none can land from here on.
+            doubt.cannot_land();
+        }
+        let first = match read(&session_key).await {
+            Ok(found) => found,
+            Err(err) => return Err(fault(doubt, err)),
+        };
+        doubt.session_seen(first.as_ref());
+        let slot_found = match read(attempt.slot_key()).await {
+            Ok(found) => found,
+            Err(err) => return Err(fault(doubt, err)),
+        };
+        let slot = match judge_slot(slot_found.as_ref(), &attempt) {
+            Ok(slot) => slot,
+            Err(err) => return Err(torn(doubt, err)),
+        };
+        if slot == SlotSeen::Held {
+            doubt.slot_held();
+        }
+        let last_found = match read(&session_key).await {
+            Ok(found) => found,
+            Err(err) => return Err(fault(doubt, err)),
+        };
+        doubt.session_seen(last_found.as_ref());
+        let last = match judge_session(last_found.as_ref(), &session) {
+            Ok(last) => last,
+            Err(err) => return Err(torn(doubt, err)),
+        };
+        match slot {
+            SlotSeen::Gone => {
+                if matches!(last, SessionSeen::Same) {
+                    // The own-commit proof, checked before anything the part key holds: the slot
+                    // is gone and the session read after it is still `Open@E`. Only this
+                    // attempt's commit removes the slot while the session is `Open@E` and no
+                    // compensation has been sent.
+                    if doubt.any() {
+                        return Ok(committed);
+                    }
+                    return Err(stop(Stop::SlotLost {
+                        key: lossy(attempt.slot_key()),
+                    }));
+                }
+                if doubt.any() {
+                    return Err(doubt.end(&upload_id, DoubtfulBatch::Commit, Stop::SessionMoved));
+                }
+                return match last {
+                    // A teardown took the slot; nothing of this attempt landed.
+                    SessionSeen::Left(refusal) => Ok(UploadPartOutcome::Refused(refusal)),
+                    SessionSeen::Same | SessionSeen::Open(_) => Err(stop(Stop::SlotLost {
+                        key: lossy(attempt.slot_key()),
+                    })),
+                };
+            }
+            SlotSeen::Rewritten => {
+                return Err(doubt.end(
+                    &upload_id,
+                    DoubtfulBatch::Commit,
+                    Stop::SlotLost {
+                        key: lossy(attempt.slot_key()),
+                    },
+                ))
+            }
+            SlotSeen::Held => {
+                if doubt.any() {
+                    // A commit of this attempt may still land: retry the same batch, which
+                    // requires the same slot bytes, so at most one of them lands. Never
+                    // compensate while it may.
+                    continue;
+                }
+                match last {
+                    SessionSeen::Same if part_now == required => {
+                        // Nothing a read can see explains the conflict.
+                    }
+                    // A same-number rival won.
+                    SessionSeen::Same => {
+                        let refusal = Refusal::OperationAborted;
+                        return compensate(store, &attempt, session, refusal).await;
+                    }
+                    // A Complete fenced and rolled the session back: the reaper does not walk an
+                    // `Open` session, so this attempt compensates under the newer epoch.
+                    SessionSeen::Open(newer) => {
+                        let refusal = Refusal::OperationAborted;
+                        return compensate(store, &attempt, newer, refusal).await;
+                    }
+                    // Not `Open` any more: the residue is the reaper's.
+                    SessionSeen::Left(refusal) => return Ok(UploadPartOutcome::Refused(refusal)),
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/// **The live-session compensation** (`0016:673`, `:1607-1620`): release the slot, delete the
+/// owned entries, and for a non-empty part install one `{chunks}` obligation naming them, under
+/// `session`, then answer `refusal`. Called only once the commit is settled as not landed and
+/// unable to land later, so the slot it releases can only be released by one of its own rounds.
+async fn compensate(
+    store: &impl MetadataStore,
+    attempt: &StagedAttempt,
+    mut session: Bytes,
+    refusal: Refusal,
+) -> Result<UploadPartOutcome, CommitError> {
+    let upload_id = attempt.upload_id();
+    let session_key = mpu_key(upload_id);
+    let mut doubt = Doubt::default();
+    // Every obligation a round of this compensation sent: its key and the bytes it puts.
+    let mut sent: Vec<(Vec<u8>, Bytes)> = Vec::new();
+    let mut rounds = 0u32;
+    loop {
+        let end = |doubt: Doubt, cause| doubt.end(upload_id, DoubtfulBatch::Compensation, cause);
+        if rounds == COMPENSATION_ROUNDS {
+            return Err(end(doubt, Stop::CompensationRoundsSpent { rounds }));
+        }
+        rounds += 1;
+        let epoch = match decode_session_record(&session) {
+            Ok(record) => record.epoch(),
+            Err(err) => return Err(end(doubt, Stop::Record(err))),
+        };
+        let obligation = match RetireObligation::part_chunks(
+            upload_id,
+            epoch,
+            attempt.part_number(),
+            attempt.attempt_id(),
+            attempt.chunks(),
+        ) {
+            Ok(obligation) => obligation,
+            Err(err) => return Err(end(doubt, Stop::Record(err))),
+        };
+        if let Some(obligation) = &obligation {
+            let put = (obligation.key(), metadata::encode(obligation.payload()));
+            if !sent.contains(&put) {
+                sent.push(put);
+            }
+        }
+        match store
+            .commit(compensation_batch(attempt, &session, obligation.as_ref()))
+            .await
+        {
+            Ok(CommitOutcome::Committed) => return Ok(UploadPartOutcome::Refused(refusal)),
+            Ok(CommitOutcome::Conflict) => {}
+            Err(fault) => match fault.downcast_ref::<CommitUnknownResult>() {
+                Some(unknown) => doubt.observe(unknown, &session),
+                None => return Err(end(doubt, Stop::Store(fault))),
+            },
+        }
+        for (key, bytes) in &sent {
+            match store.get(key).await {
+                Ok(Some(found)) if found == *bytes => {
+                    return Ok(UploadPartOutcome::Refused(refusal))
+                }
+                Ok(Some(_)) => {
+                    return Err(end(doubt, Stop::ObligationKeyTaken { key: lossy(key) }))
+                }
+                Ok(None) => {}
+                Err(fault) => return Err(end(doubt, Stop::Store(fault))),
+            }
+        }
+        let slot = match store.get(attempt.slot_key()).await {
+            Ok(found) => match judge_slot(found.as_ref(), attempt) {
+                Ok(slot) => slot,
+                Err(err) => return Err(end(doubt, Stop::Record(err))),
+            },
+            Err(fault) => return Err(end(doubt, Stop::Store(fault))),
+        };
+        if slot == SlotSeen::Held {
+            doubt.slot_held();
+        }
+        let found = match store.get(&session_key).await {
+            Ok(found) => found,
+            Err(fault) => return Err(end(doubt, Stop::Store(fault))),
+        };
+        doubt.session_seen(found.as_ref());
+        let now = match judge_session(found.as_ref(), &session) {
+            Ok(now) => now,
+            Err(err) => return Err(end(doubt, Stop::Record(err))),
+        };
+        match slot {
+            SlotSeen::Gone => {
+                // The slot gone, and the session read after it still the bytes a doubtful round
+                // required: no commit of this attempt is outstanding, so that round landed.
+                if doubt.required(found.as_ref()) {
+                    return Ok(UploadPartOutcome::Refused(refusal));
+                }
+                if doubt.any() {
+                    return Err(end(doubt, Stop::SessionMoved));
+                }
+                return match now {
+                    SessionSeen::Left(left) => Ok(UploadPartOutcome::Refused(left)),
+                    SessionSeen::Same | SessionSeen::Open(_) => Err(stopped(
+                        upload_id,
+                        Stop::SlotLost {
+                            key: lossy(attempt.slot_key()),
+                        },
+                    )),
+                };
+            }
+            SlotSeen::Rewritten => {
+                return Err(end(
+                    doubt,
+                    Stop::SlotLost {
+                        key: lossy(attempt.slot_key()),
+                    },
+                ))
+            }
+            SlotSeen::Held => match now {
+                // Retry; a round still in flight requires the same slot bytes, so at most one
+                // lands.
+                SessionSeen::Same => {}
+                // The epoch chase: compensate again under the newer `Open` epoch.
+                SessionSeen::Open(newer) => session = newer,
+                SessionSeen::Left(left) => {
+                    if doubt.any() {
+                        return Err(end(doubt, Stop::SessionMoved));
+                    }
+                    return Ok(UploadPartOutcome::Refused(left));
+                }
+            },
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/// **`UploadPart`, whole** (#657): reserve a slot, stage the body ([`stage_part`]), then commit
+/// it ([`commit_part`]), on one runtime whose clock owns the attempt's leases. A staging refusal
+/// is answered as it is; a staging error is [`UploadPartError::Stage`] and no commit is
+/// attempted. `max_staged_chunks` is the cumulative ceiling [`commit_part`] checks.
+///
+/// No production path calls this yet (the S3 verb is #669).
+pub async fn upload_part<B>(
+    store: &impl MetadataStore,
+    chunk_store: &impl PlacementChunkStore,
+    runtime: &mut impl StageRuntime,
+    request: &StageRequest<'_>,
+    max_staged_chunks: u32,
+    body: B,
+) -> Result<UploadPartOutcome, UploadPartError>
+where
+    B: Stream<Item = wyrd_traits::Result<Bytes>> + Unpin,
+{
+    match stage_part(store, chunk_store, runtime, request, body).await {
+        Ok(StageOutcome::Staged(attempt)) => {
+            commit_part(store, &*runtime, *attempt, max_staged_chunks)
+                .await
+                .map_err(UploadPartError::Commit)
+        }
+        Ok(StageOutcome::Refused(refusal)) => Ok(UploadPartOutcome::Refused(refusal)),
+        Err(err) => Err(UploadPartError::Stage(err)),
+    }
+}
